' WELCOME.SPK - the Welcome Wagon, for the central host (STARTHERE).
'
' Every machine runs a Chat service (port 6667), and the Chat program
' connects to its own machine's, in #general, out of the box: so somebody
' new who opens Chat finds an empty room. The Welcome Wagon is in every one
' of those rooms. It says hello to newcomers (once), tells them what this
' machine serves (the same list as SimHost's front page), and links the
' rooms into one: everybody in #general anywhere is in #general everywhere
' somebody is, under their own name.
'
' How it keeps up with machines that come and go all the time:
'   * It looks round the network every few seconds (NET.Machines). A new
'     machine gets the bot in its room, as StartHereBot, or StartHereBo2,
'     3... when the name is taken. A machine missing from two looks in a row
'     has gone: its room, its people and their stand-ins go too. (A machine
'     that leaves doesn't close its connections: they just go quiet.)
'   * Each look round, it asks every room who is there (WHO) and believes
'     the answer: anybody it missed coming or going is put right.
'   * The stand-ins (a connection under each person's name in each other
'     room with somebody in it, saying what they say) are worked out again
'     from that four times a second: missing ones made, extra ones closed.
'   * A connection that doesn't get through in time is given up and tried
'     again; so is a room that has said nothing for three looks round.
'
' One clock (Work) changes everything. The network's events, the dialler
' and the look round only hand things to it (one Add each), so nothing is
' changed by two at once; and each thing it is handed is dealt with inside
' its own TRY, so one bad line is noted, not fatal.
'
' Connections are closed without QUIT: the stock Chat service can crash on
' a QUIT followed by a close (see SIM95-NOTES.md), never on a plain close.
' Lines go one a tick on each connection, as the service can shuffle lines
' that arrive together.
'
' In a room:
'   sites    the sites here, one a line
'   who      who is in the conversation, and where
'   unlink   this room stays to itself (C:\WELCOME\UNLINK.TXT); link undoes it
'   bye      the bot leaves that machine's room, for good (C:\WELCOME\OPTOUT.TXT)
' Settings, in C:\WELCOME\WELCOME.INI:
'   channel=#general    the room
'   every=10            seconds between looks round the network
' Whom it has greeted is in C:\WELCOME\SEEN.TXT (machine|nick).

CONST HOME = "C:\WELCOME"
CONST BOTNICK = "StartHereBot"
CONST SETTLE = 1500               ' greet and link somebody this long after they come in (ms)
CONST QUIET = 15000               ' sites or who at most this often in one room (ms)
CONST MOST = 200                  ' lines kept in the window
CONST MOSTLINKS = 400             ' stand-ins at most, all told
CONST MOSTDIALS = 4               ' connections on their way at once
CONST MISSES = 2                  ' looks round a machine may miss before it has gone
CONST WAITCONNECT = 12000         ' a connection not through by then is given up (ms)
CONST RETRY = 300000              ' a machine whose Chat service never answered: again after (ms)
CONST RETRYSOON = 10000           ' ...one whose did (it may have crashed) (ms)
CONST CLASHWAIT = 60000           ' a taken name is tried again after (ms)

VAR EOL AS String
VAR SEP AS String
VAR win AS GUI_Window
VAR journal AS GUI_ListBox
VAR sock AS NET_Socket
VAR worker AS GUI_Timer
VAR dialer AS GUI_Timer
VAR scanner AS GUI_Timer
VAR noted AS Array OF String

VAR channel AS String
VAR every AS Integer              ' seconds between looks round
VAR here AS String                ' this machine as people type it: starthere
VAR seen AS Array OF String       ' MACHINE|nick: greeted already
VAR greeted AS Integer
VAR serial AS Integer             ' for tags
VAR statusAt AS Integer

' Handed to the worker, one Add at a time.
VAR inbox AS Array OF String      ' tag, SEP, then a line, or Chr(1) + CONNECTED / FAILED / CLOSED
VAR fresh AS Array OF NET_Connection
VAR dialQ AS Array OF String      ' tag, SEP, address: for the dialler
VAR flights AS Array OF Integer   ' when each connection on its way set out
VAR scanned AS Array OF String    ' the last look round: NAME ADDRESS MS
VAR scanSerial AS Integer
VAR doneSerial AS Integer
VAR scanning AS Bool
VAR scanAt AS Integer
VAR working AS Bool
VAR workingAt AS Integer

' The open connections, and the lines waiting for each (the worker's own).
VAR cTag AS Array OF String
VAR cConn AS Array OF NET_Connection
VAR outTag AS Array OF String
VAR outText AS Array OF String

' The rooms, one a machine (this one's too, as localhost). States:
'   idle (to dial) - dialing - naming (NICK sent) - in (JOINed)
'   nochat (nobody answered) - gone (off the network) - left (said bye)
VAR mName AS Array OF String
VAR mAddr AS Array OF String
VAR mState AS Array OF String
VAR mTag AS Array OF String       ' its connection now: R:<n>
VAR mNick AS Array OF String      ' the bot's name there
VAR mSince AS Array OF Integer
VAR mHeard AS Array OF Integer    ' when it last heard from the room
VAR mMissed AS Array OF Integer   ' looks round missed in a row
VAR mTries AS Array OF Integer    ' names tried
VAR mListed AS Array OF Integer   ' when it last listed sites or people there
VAR mLinked AS Array OF Bool
VAR mTold AS Array OF Bool        ' told (since it started) the room is linked
VAR mWasIn AS Array OF Bool
VAR mFirst AS Array OF Bool       ' the first WHO since it came in is still to come

' The people in the rooms (not the bot, not stand-ins).
VAR pRoom AS Array OF String
VAR pNick AS Array OF String
VAR pAt AS Array OF Integer
VAR pDone AS Array OF Bool        ' settled: greeted (or not) and linked
VAR pQuiet AS Array OF Bool       ' not to be greeted (there before the bot came)

' Stand-ins: in a room, for a person (their room and name), under a name.
'   dialing - naming - in - closing (CLOSE queued) - cancel (close when through)
VAR sTag AS Array OF String       ' S:<n>
VAR sRoom AS Array OF String
VAR sOwner AS Array OF String
VAR sOwnerNick AS Array OF String
VAR sNick AS Array OF String
VAR sState AS Array OF String
VAR sSince AS Array OF Integer

' Names taken elsewhere: owner room|nick|room, and when; told already.
VAR clashKey AS Array OF String
VAR clashAt AS Array OF Integer
VAR told AS Array OF String

' Recent renames (room, old, new, when): a NICK can come before the JOIN it followed.
VAR nRoom AS Array OF String
VAR nOld AS Array OF String
VAR nNew AS Array OF String
VAR nAt AS Array OF Integer

SUB Main ()
    VAR line AS String
    EOL = Chr(10)
    SEP = Chr(9)
    IF NOT FS.Exists(HOME) THEN FS.MakeDir(HOME)
    channel = "#general"
    every = 10
    FOR EACH line IN ReadOr(HOME + "\WELCOME.INI", "").Lines()
        IF line.StartsWith("channel=") THEN channel = line.Substring(8, line.Length - 8).Trim().Lower()
        IF line.StartsWith("every=") THEN every = MATH.Max(1, Int(Val(line.Substring(6, line.Length - 6))))
    NEXT
    IF NOT channel.StartsWith("#") THEN channel = "#" + channel
    here = NET.HostName.Split(".")[0].Lower()
    FOR EACH line IN ReadOr(HOME + "\SEEN.TXT", "").Lines()
        IF line <> "" THEN seen.Add(line)
    NEXT

    win = GUI_Window.New("Welcome Wagon", 480, 260)
    win.Icon = "chat"
    win.onClose = Win_OnClose
    journal = GUI_ListBox.New(win)
    journal.SetBounds(6, 6, 468, 226)
    sock = NET_Socket.New()
    sock.onMessage = Conn_OnMessage
    sock.onClose = Conn_OnClose
    ' this machine's own room too: it is where everybody meets
    AddRoom(NET.HostName.Upper(), "localhost")
    worker = GUI_Timer.New(win)
    worker.Interval = 250
    worker.onTick = Worker_OnTick
    worker.Start()
    dialer = GUI_Timer.New(win)
    dialer.Interval = 100
    dialer.onTick = Dialer_OnTick
    dialer.Start()
    scanner = GUI_Timer.New(win)
    scanner.Interval = 1000
    scanner.onTick = Scanner_OnTick
    scanner.Start()
    Note("Greeting people in " + channel + " on every machine, for http://" + here + "/, and linking the rooms")
    Status()
    win.Show()
END SUB

SUB Win_OnClose ()
    SYS.Exit(0)
END SUB

FUNCTION ReadOr (path AS String, fallback AS String) AS String
    IF FS.Exists(path) THEN RETURN FS.Read(path)
    RETURN fallback
END FUNCTION

SUB Note (text AS String)
    noted.Add(TIME.Clock + "  " + text)
    IF noted.Count > MOST THEN noted.RemoveAt(0)
    journal.Items = noted
    journal.ScrollToEnd()
END SUB

SUB Status ()
    VAR n AS Integer
    VAR s AS String
    FOR EACH s IN mState
        IF s = "in" THEN n = n + 1
    NEXT
    win.Status = Str(n) + " room" + Plural(n) + " open  -  " + Str(pRoom.Count) + " " + People(pRoom.Count) + " in them  -  " + Str(sTag.Count) + " stand-in" + Plural(sTag.Count) + "  -  " + Str(greeted) + " greeted since it started"
END SUB

FUNCTION Plural (n AS Integer) AS String
    IF n = 1 THEN RETURN ""
    RETURN "s"
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION People (n AS Integer) AS String
    IF n = 1 THEN RETURN "person"
    RETURN "people"
END FUNCTION

' The machine as people say it: newbie, starthere
FUNCTION Called (room AS String) AS String
    RETURN room.Split(".")[0].Lower()
END FUNCTION

' Is the machine (by computer name) in the file, one name a line?
FUNCTION InFile (path AS String, name AS String) AS Bool
    VAR line AS String
    FOR EACH line IN ReadOr(path, "").Lines()
        IF line.Trim().Lower() = Called(name) THEN RETURN TRUE
    NEXT
    RETURN FALSE
END FUNCTION

' The lines of text, without the one that is name.
FUNCTION Without (text AS String, name AS String) AS String
    VAR out AS String
    VAR line AS String
    FOR EACH line IN text.Lines()
        IF line.Trim() <> "" AND line.Trim().Lower() <> name.Lower() THEN out = out + line.Trim() + EOL
    NEXT
    RETURN out
END FUNCTION

' ================================================================ the hand-overs

SUB Conn_OnMessage (conn AS NET_Connection, message AS String)
    inbox.Add(conn.Tag + SEP + message)
END SUB

SUB Conn_OnClose (conn AS NET_Connection)
    inbox.Add(conn.Tag + SEP + Chr(1) + "CLOSED")
END SUB

' Every few seconds: who is on the network.
SUB Scanner_OnTick ()
    TRY
        IF scanning AND SYS.Ticks - scanAt < 8000 THEN RETURN
        IF scanAt <> 0 AND SYS.Ticks - scanAt < every * 1000 THEN RETURN
        scanning = TRUE
        scanAt = MATH.Max(1, SYS.Ticks)
        scanned = NET.Machines()
        scanSerial = scanSerial + 1
        scanning = FALSE
    CATCH err
        scanning = FALSE
    END TRY
END SUB

' A few connections on their way at once, so one to a machine that has
' just gone can't hold the others up. (A failed Connect spoils the rest of
' its handler, so after it there are only two statements and the end of
' the handler: see SIM95-NOTES.md.)
SUB Dialer_OnTick ()
    TRY
        DialOne()
    CATCH err
    END TRY
END SUB

SUB DialOne ()
    VAR req AS String
    VAR tag AS String
    VAR conn AS NET_Connection
    VAR started AS Integer
    VAR k AS Integer
    FOR k = flights.Count - 1 TO 0 STEP -1
        IF SYS.Ticks - flights[k] > WAITCONNECT THEN flights.RemoveAt(k)
    NEXT
    IF flights.Count >= MOSTDIALS THEN RETURN
    ' the next one still wanted (a room or stand-in given up on is skipped)
    req = ""
    WHILE dialQ.Count > 0 AND req = ""
        req = dialQ[0]
        dialQ.RemoveAt(0)
        tag = req.Substring(0, req.IndexOf(SEP))
        IF NOT mTag.Contains(tag) AND NOT sTag.Contains(tag) THEN req = ""
    END WHILE
    IF req = "" THEN RETURN
    started = SYS.Ticks
    flights.Add(started)
    TRY
        conn = sock.Connect(req.Substring(req.IndexOf(SEP) + 1, req.Length - req.IndexOf(SEP) - 1), 6667)
        conn.Tag = tag
        fresh.Add(conn)
        inbox.Add(tag + SEP + Chr(1) + "CONNECTED")
        k = flights.IndexOf(started)
        IF k >= 0 THEN flights.RemoveAt(k)
    CATCH err
        inbox.Add(tag + SEP + Chr(1) + "FAILED")
        flights.RemoveAt(MATH.Max(0, flights.IndexOf(started)))
    END TRY
END SUB

' ================================================================ the worker

SUB Worker_OnTick ()
    IF working AND SYS.Ticks - workingAt < 5000 THEN RETURN
    working = TRUE
    workingAt = SYS.Ticks
    TRY
        Work()
    CATCH err
        Note("Trouble: " + err)
    END TRY
    working = FALSE
END SUB

SUB Work ()
    VAR item AS String
    VAR shown AS String
    VAR n AS Integer
    ' new connections into the table (or closed, if nothing wants them now)
    WHILE fresh.Count > 0
        TakeIn(fresh[0])
        fresh.RemoveAt(0)
    END WHILE
    ' what came in, in order
    WHILE inbox.Count > 0 AND n < 300
        item = inbox[0]
        inbox.RemoveAt(0)
        n = n + 1
        TRY
            Deal(item)
        CATCH err
            shown = item.Replace(SEP, " ").Replace(Chr(1), "")
            Note("Trouble with " + shown.Substring(0, MATH.Min(60, shown.Length)) + ": " + err)
        END TRY
    END WHILE
    IF scanSerial <> doneSerial THEN
        doneSerial = scanSerial
        Census()
    END IF
    Timeouts()
    SettleIn()
    Reconcile()
    SendSome()
    IF SYS.Ticks - statusAt > 1000 THEN
        statusAt = SYS.Ticks
        Status()
    END IF
END SUB

SUB TakeIn (conn AS NET_Connection)
    IF mTag.Contains(conn.Tag) OR sTag.Contains(conn.Tag) THEN
        cTag.Add(conn.Tag)
        cConn.Add(conn)
    ELSE
        ' (given up on while it connected)
        TRY
            conn.Close()
        CATCH err
        END TRY
    END IF
END SUB

SUB Deal (item AS String)
    VAR tag AS String
    VAR msg AS String
    IF NOT item.Contains(SEP) THEN RETURN
    tag = item.Substring(0, item.IndexOf(SEP))
    msg = item.Substring(item.IndexOf(SEP) + 1, item.Length - item.IndexOf(SEP) - 1)
    IF tag = "" THEN RETURN
    IF mTag.Contains(tag) THEN
        RoomHeard(mTag.IndexOf(tag), tag, msg)
    ELSEIF sTag.Contains(tag) THEN
        StandInHeard(sTag.IndexOf(tag), tag, msg)
    ELSEIF msg <> Chr(1) + "CLOSED" AND NOT outTag.Contains(tag) THEN
        ' a connection nothing wants any more (and with nothing left to say)
        Forget(tag)
    END IF
END SUB

' ================================================================ connections

FUNCTION ConnOf (tag AS String) AS Integer
    RETURN cTag.IndexOf(tag)
END FUNCTION

' Out of the table, and closed.
SUB Forget (tag AS String)
    VAR k AS Integer
    k = cTag.IndexOf(tag)
    IF k < 0 THEN RETURN
    TRY
        cConn[k].Close()
    CATCH err
    END TRY
    cTag.RemoveAt(k)
    cConn.RemoveAt(k)
END SUB

SUB SendNow (tag AS String, line AS String)
    VAR k AS Integer
    k = cTag.IndexOf(tag)
    IF k < 0 THEN RETURN
    TRY
        cConn[k].Send(line)
    CATCH err
    END TRY
END SUB

' A line for a connection, in its turn: one a tick for each connection.
' Chr(1) + "CLOSE" closes it; Chr(1) + anything else is sent as it is;
' anything else is said in the room.
SUB Queue (tag AS String, text AS String)
    outTag.Add(tag)
    outText.Add(text)
END SUB

SUB SendSome ()
    VAR k AS Integer
    VAR done AS String
    VAR tag AS String
    VAR text AS String
    VAR s AS Integer
    done = ","
    k = 0
    WHILE k < outTag.Count
        IF done.Contains("," + outTag[k] + ",") THEN
            k = k + 1
        ELSE
            tag = outTag[k]
            text = outText[k]
            outTag.RemoveAt(k)
            outText.RemoveAt(k)
            IF ConnOf(tag) >= 0 THEN
                done = done + tag + ","
                IF text = Chr(1) + "CLOSE" THEN
                    Forget(tag)
                    s = sTag.IndexOf(tag)
                    IF s >= 0 THEN DropStandIn(s)
                ELSEIF text.StartsWith(Chr(1)) THEN
                    SendNow(tag, text.Substring(1, text.Length - 1))
                ELSE
                    SendNow(tag, "MSG " + channel + " " + text)
                END IF
            END IF
        END IF
    END WHILE
END SUB

' ================================================================ the network

' What the look round found: new machines get a room; machines missing
' from it twice have gone; every room is asked who is there.
SUB Census ()
    VAR m AS String
    VAR p AS Array OF String
    VAR i AS Integer
    VAR found AS String
    found = ","
    FOR EACH m IN scanned
        p = m.Split(" ")
        IF p.Count < 2 THEN CONTINUE
        IF p[0].Upper() = NET.HostName.Upper() OR p[1] = NET.LocalAddress THEN CONTINUE
        found = found + p[0].Upper() + ","
        i = mName.IndexOf(p[0].Upper())
        IF i < 0 THEN
            AddRoom(p[0].Upper(), p[1])
            Note("Found " + p[0])
        ELSE
            mMissed[i] = 0
            IF mAddr[i] <> p[1] THEN
                ' the same name at a new address: a new machine, really
                mAddr[i] = p[1]
                IF mState[i] <> "left" AND mState[i] <> "gone" THEN RoomDown(i, "idle")
            END IF
            IF mState[i] = "gone" THEN
                SetState(i, "idle")
                Note(mName[i] + " is back")
            END IF
        END IF
    NEXT
    FOR i = 0 TO mName.Count - 1
        IF IsHub(i) OR found.Contains("," + mName[i] + ",") THEN CONTINUE
        mMissed[i] = mMissed[i] + 1
        IF mMissed[i] >= MISSES AND mState[i] <> "gone" AND mState[i] <> "left" THEN
            Note(mName[i] + " has left the network")
            RoomDown(i, "gone")
        END IF
    NEXT
    ' who is really there (the answer puts right anything missed)
    FOR i = 0 TO mName.Count - 1
        IF mState[i] = "in" THEN Queue(mTag[i], Chr(1) + "WHO " + channel)
    NEXT
END SUB

SUB AddRoom (name AS String, addr AS String)
    mName.Add(name)
    mAddr.Add(addr)
    mState.Add("idle")
    mTag.Add("")
    mNick.Add(BOTNICK)
    mSince.Add(0)
    mHeard.Add(0)
    mMissed.Add(0)
    mTries.Add(0)
    mListed.Add(0)
    mLinked.Add(NOT InFile(HOME + "\UNLINK.TXT", name))
    mTold.Add(FALSE)
    mWasIn.Add(FALSE)
    mFirst.Add(FALSE)
    IF InFile(HOME + "\OPTOUT.TXT", name) THEN mState[mState.Count - 1] = "left"
END SUB

SUB SetState (i AS Integer, s AS String)
    mState[i] = s
    mSince[i] = SYS.Ticks
END SUB

FUNCTION IsHub (i AS Integer) AS Bool
    RETURN mAddr[i] = "localhost"
END FUNCTION

' The name for the bot, try n: StartHereBot, StartHereBo2... then any.
FUNCTION NameTry (n AS Integer) AS String
    IF n = 0 THEN RETURN BOTNICK
    IF n < 9 THEN RETURN BOTNICK.Substring(0, 11) + Str(n + 1)
    RETURN "SHBot" + Str(1000 + Rnd(9000))
END FUNCTION

SUB Dial (i AS Integer)
    serial = serial + 1
    mTag[i] = "R:" + Str(serial)
    SetState(i, "dialing")
    mTries[i] = 0
    dialQ.Add(mTag[i] + SEP + mAddr[i])
END SUB

' Room i is closed: its connection, its people, the stand-ins in it.
SUB RoomDown (i AS Integer, state AS String)
    VAR k AS Integer
    IF mTag[i] <> "" THEN Forget(mTag[i])
    mTag[i] = ""
    FOR k = pRoom.Count - 1 TO 0 STEP -1
        IF pRoom[k] = mName[i] THEN RemovePerson(k)
    NEXT
    FOR k = sTag.Count - 1 TO 0 STEP -1
        IF sRoom[k] = mName[i] THEN
            Forget(sTag[k])
            DropStandIn(k)
        END IF
    NEXT
    ClearClashes(mName[i])
    SetState(i, state)
END SUB

' Rooms that have waited long enough, connections that have taken too long,
' rooms gone quiet, stand-ins stuck on the way.
SUB Timeouts ()
    VAR i AS Integer
    VAR k AS Integer
    VAR now AS Integer
    now = SYS.Ticks
    FOR i = 0 TO mName.Count - 1
        SELECT CASE mState[i]
            CASE "idle"
                IF now - mSince[i] >= 1000 AND mMissed[i] = 0 THEN Dial(i)
            CASE "dialing"
                IF now - mSince[i] > WAITCONNECT THEN RoomDown(i, "idle")
            CASE "naming"
                IF now - mSince[i] > WAITCONNECT THEN RoomDown(i, "idle")
            CASE "in"
                IF now - mHeard[i] > every * 3000 + 10000 THEN
                    Note("Nothing from " + mName[i] + " for a while: trying again")
                    RoomDown(i, "idle")
                END IF
            CASE "nochat"
                IF now - mSince[i] > RETRY OR (mWasIn[i] AND now - mSince[i] > RETRYSOON) THEN SetState(i, "idle")
        END SELECT
    NEXT
    FOR k = sTag.Count - 1 TO 0 STEP -1
        IF (sState[k] = "dialing" OR sState[k] = "cancel" OR sState[k] = "naming") AND now - sSince[k] > WAITCONNECT THEN
            Forget(sTag[k])
            DropStandIn(k)
        ELSEIF sState[k] = "closing" AND now - sSince[k] > 10000 THEN
            Forget(sTag[k])
            DropStandIn(k)
        END IF
    NEXT
END SUB

' ================================================================ a room's lines

SUB RoomHeard (i AS Integer, tag AS String, msg AS String)
    VAR p AS Array OF String
    VAR cut AS Integer
    VAR text AS String
    mHeard[i] = SYS.Ticks
    IF msg = Chr(1) + "CONNECTED" THEN
        SetState(i, "naming")
        mTries[i] = 0
        SendNow(tag, "NICK " + NameTry(0))
        RETURN
    END IF
    IF msg = Chr(1) + "FAILED" THEN
        RoomDown(i, "nochat")
        RETURN
    END IF
    IF msg = Chr(1) + "CLOSED" THEN
        IF mState[i] = "in" THEN Note("The room on " + mName[i] + " closed")
        RoomDown(i, "idle")
        RETURN
    END IF
    p = msg.Split(" ")
    SELECT CASE p[0]
        CASE "OK"
            ' its name is taken: now into the room
            IF msg.StartsWith("OK You are now ") THEN
                mNick[i] = msg.Substring(15, msg.Length - 15).Trim()
                IF mState[i] = "naming" THEN
                    SetState(i, "in")
                    mWasIn[i] = TRUE
                    mFirst[i] = TRUE
                    Queue(tag, Chr(1) + "JOIN " + channel)
                END IF
            END IF
        CASE "ERR"
            ' the name is somebody's: the next one
            IF mState[i] = "naming" AND (msg.Contains("Nick in use") OR msg.Contains("Bad nick")) THEN
                mTries[i] = mTries[i] + 1
                SendNow(tag, "NICK " + NameTry(mTries[i]))
            END IF
        CASE "WHO"
            IF p.Count >= 2 THEN
                IF p[1] = channel THEN
                    IF p.Count >= 3 THEN
                        Sync(i, p[2])
                    ELSE
                        Sync(i, "")
                    END IF
                END IF
            END IF
        CASE "JOIN"
            IF p.Count >= 3 THEN
                IF p[1] = channel AND NOT Ours(i, p[2]) THEN Arrive(i, p[2], FALSE)
            END IF
        CASE "PART"
            IF p.Count >= 3 THEN
                IF p[1] = channel AND NOT Ours(i, p[2]) THEN Leave(i, p[2])
            END IF
        CASE "NICK"
            IF p.Count >= 4 THEN
                IF NOT Ours(i, p[2]) AND NOT Ours(i, p[3]) THEN Renamed(i, p[2], p[3])
            END IF
        CASE "MSG"
            IF p.Count >= 4 THEN
                IF p[1] = channel AND NOT Ours(i, p[2]) THEN
                    cut = p[0].Length + p[1].Length + p[2].Length + 3
                    text = msg.Substring(cut, msg.Length - cut)
                    Arrive(i, p[2], FALSE)
                    Relay(i, p[2], text)
                    Obey(i, p[2], text)
                END IF
            END IF
    END SELECT
END SUB

' The bot itself, or one of its stand-ins, in room i.
FUNCTION Ours (i AS Integer, nick AS String) AS Bool
    VAR k AS Integer
    IF nick.Lower() = mNick[i].Lower() THEN RETURN TRUE
    FOR k = 0 TO sTag.Count - 1
        IF sRoom[k] = mName[i] AND sNick[k].Lower() = nick.Lower() THEN RETURN TRUE
    NEXT
    RETURN FALSE
END FUNCTION

' The answer to WHO: everybody there now. Newcomers are added; anybody no
' longer there (and not just come) is gone.
SUB Sync (i AS Integer, list AS String)
    VAR names AS String
    VAR n AS String
    VAR k AS Integer
    VAR quiet AS Bool
    ' the regulars on this machine, there when the bot came: no hello for them
    quiet = mFirst[i] AND IsHub(i)
    mFirst[i] = FALSE
    names = ","
    FOR EACH n IN list.Split(",")
        IF n = "" OR Ours(i, n) THEN CONTINUE
        names = names + n.Lower() + ","
        Arrive(i, n, quiet)
    NEXT
    FOR k = pRoom.Count - 1 TO 0 STEP -1
        IF pRoom[k] = mName[i] AND NOT names.Contains("," + pNick[k].Lower() + ",") AND SYS.Ticks - pAt[k] > 3000 THEN
            RemovePerson(k)
            ClearClashes(mName[i])
        END IF
    NEXT
END SUB

' ================================================================ people

SUB Arrive (i AS Integer, nick AS String, quiet AS Bool)
    nick = Current(mName[i], nick)
    IF PersonAt(mName[i], nick) >= 0 THEN RETURN
    pRoom.Add(mName[i])
    pNick.Add(nick)
    pAt.Add(SYS.Ticks)
    pDone.Add(FALSE)
    pQuiet.Add(quiet)
END SUB

SUB Leave (i AS Integer, nick AS String)
    VAR k AS Integer
    k = PersonAt(mName[i], nick)
    IF k < 0 THEN RETURN
    RemovePerson(k)
    ' their name is free here now
    ClearClashes(mName[i])
END SUB

SUB RemovePerson (k AS Integer)
    pRoom.RemoveAt(k)
    pNick.RemoveAt(k)
    pAt.RemoveAt(k)
    pDone.RemoveAt(k)
    pQuiet.RemoveAt(k)
END SUB

FUNCTION PersonAt (room AS String, nick AS String) AS Integer
    VAR k AS Integer
    FOR k = 0 TO pRoom.Count - 1
        IF pRoom[k] = room AND pNick[k].Lower() = nick.Lower() THEN RETURN k
    NEXT
    RETURN -1
END FUNCTION

' Somebody in room i changed their name: their stand-ins do too.
SUB Renamed (i AS Integer, old AS String, nick AS String)
    VAR k AS Integer
    VAR h AS Integer
    FOR k = nAt.Count - 1 TO 0 STEP -1
        IF SYS.Ticks - nAt[k] > 10000 THEN
            nRoom.RemoveAt(k)
            nOld.RemoveAt(k)
            nNew.RemoveAt(k)
            nAt.RemoveAt(k)
        END IF
    NEXT
    nRoom.Add(mName[i])
    nOld.Add(old)
    nNew.Add(nick)
    nAt.Add(SYS.Ticks)
    h = PersonAt(mName[i], old)
    IF h < 0 THEN RETURN
    pNick[h] = nick
    FOR k = 0 TO sTag.Count - 1
        IF sOwner[k] = mName[i] AND sOwnerNick[k].Lower() = old.Lower() THEN
            sOwnerNick[k] = nick
            IF sState[k] = "naming" OR sState[k] = "in" THEN
                sNick[k] = nick
                Queue(sTag[k], Chr(1) + "NICK " + nick)
            ELSEIF sState[k] = "dialing" THEN
                sNick[k] = nick
            END IF
        END IF
    NEXT
    ' names have changed here: anything that clashed may not now
    ClearClashes(mName[i])
END SUB

' The name somebody has now, after any renames in the last few seconds.
FUNCTION Current (room AS String, nick AS String) AS String
    VAR k AS Integer
    FOR k = 0 TO nRoom.Count - 1
        IF nRoom[k] = room AND nOld[k].Lower() = nick.Lower() AND SYS.Ticks - nAt[k] <= 10000 THEN nick = nNew[k]
    NEXT
    RETURN nick
END FUNCTION

' Somebody who came in a moment ago (time for their NICK to catch up):
' hello, once, and from now on they are linked.
SUB SettleIn ()
    VAR k AS Integer
    FOR k = 0 TO pRoom.Count - 1
        IF NOT pDone[k] AND SYS.Ticks - pAt[k] >= SETTLE THEN
            pDone[k] = TRUE
            IF NOT pQuiet[k] THEN Greet(mName.IndexOf(pRoom[k]), pNick[k])
        END IF
    NEXT
END SUB

' ================================================================ linking

' Room i shares the conversation: the bot is in it, and it isn't unlinked.
FUNCTION Linked (i AS Integer) AS Bool
    IF i < 0 THEN RETURN FALSE
    RETURN mLinked[i] AND mState[i] = "in"
END FUNCTION

' Linked, on the network at the last look, with somebody settled in it.
FUNCTION Active (i AS Integer) AS Bool
    VAR k AS Integer
    IF NOT Linked(i) THEN RETURN FALSE
    IF mMissed[i] > 0 THEN RETURN FALSE
    FOR k = 0 TO pRoom.Count - 1
        IF pRoom[k] = mName[i] AND pDone[k] THEN RETURN TRUE
    NEXT
    RETURN FALSE
END FUNCTION

' Settled people in linked rooms other than room.
FUNCTION Elsewhere (room AS String) AS Integer
    VAR k AS Integer
    VAR n AS Integer
    FOR k = 0 TO pRoom.Count - 1
        IF pRoom[k] <> room AND pDone[k] AND Linked(mName.IndexOf(pRoom[k])) THEN n = n + 1
    NEXT
    RETURN n
END FUNCTION

' Every settled person in a linked room has a stand-in in every other
' active room; nobody else has one.
SUB Reconcile ()
    VAR k AS Integer
    VAR h AS Integer
    VAR j AS Integer
    VAR owner AS Integer
    VAR want AS Bool
    ' stand-ins no longer wanted
    FOR k = sTag.Count - 1 TO 0 STEP -1
        IF sState[k] = "closing" OR sState[k] = "cancel" THEN CONTINUE
        h = PersonAt(sOwner[k], sOwnerNick[k])
        want = h >= 0
        IF want THEN want = pDone[h] AND sOwner[k] <> sRoom[k] AND Linked(mName.IndexOf(sOwner[k])) AND Active(mName.IndexOf(sRoom[k]))
        IF NOT want THEN EndStandIn(k)
    NEXT
    ' and ones that are wanted
    FOR h = 0 TO pRoom.Count - 1
        IF NOT pDone[h] THEN CONTINUE
        owner = mName.IndexOf(pRoom[h])
        IF NOT Linked(owner) THEN CONTINUE
        FOR j = 0 TO mName.Count - 1
            IF j = owner OR NOT Active(j) THEN CONTINUE
            IF HasStandIn(pRoom[h], pNick[h], mName[j]) OR Clashed(pRoom[h], pNick[h], mName[j]) THEN CONTINUE
            IF sTag.Count >= MOSTLINKS THEN RETURN
            serial = serial + 1
            sTag.Add("S:" + Str(serial))
            sRoom.Add(mName[j])
            sOwner.Add(pRoom[h])
            sOwnerNick.Add(pNick[h])
            sNick.Add(pNick[h])
            sState.Add("dialing")
            sSince.Add(SYS.Ticks)
            dialQ.Add("S:" + Str(serial) + SEP + mAddr[j])
        NEXT
    NEXT
    ' a room linked to somebody, whose people haven't been told
    FOR j = 0 TO mName.Count - 1
        IF NOT mTold[j] THEN
            IF Active(j) AND Elsewhere(mName[j]) > 0 THEN
                mTold[j] = TRUE
                Say(j, "This room is linked to " + channel + " on every machine: people elsewhere on the network see what's said here. Say unlink to keep it to this machine.")
            END IF
        END IF
    NEXT
END SUB

FUNCTION HasStandIn (owner AS String, nick AS String, room AS String) AS Bool
    VAR k AS Integer
    FOR k = 0 TO sTag.Count - 1
        IF sOwner[k] = owner AND sOwnerNick[k].Lower() = nick.Lower() AND sRoom[k] = room THEN RETURN TRUE
    NEXT
    RETURN FALSE
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION Clashed (owner AS String, nick AS String, room AS String) AS Bool
    VAR k AS Integer
    k = clashKey.IndexOf(owner + "|" + nick.Lower() + "|" + room)
    IF k < 0 THEN RETURN FALSE
    RETURN SYS.Ticks - clashAt[k] < CLASHWAIT
END FUNCTION

' Names in room have changed (somebody left, or renamed): try again there.
SUB ClearClashes (room AS String)
    VAR k AS Integer
    FOR k = clashKey.Count - 1 TO 0 STEP -1
        IF clashKey[k].EndsWith("|" + room) THEN
            clashKey.RemoveAt(k)
            clashAt.RemoveAt(k)
        END IF
    NEXT
END SUB

' Stand-in k goes: closed in its turn (after anything it still has to say),
' or as soon as it is through, if it is on its way.
SUB EndStandIn (k AS Integer)
    IF sState[k] = "dialing" THEN
        sState[k] = "cancel"
        sSince[k] = SYS.Ticks
    ELSEIF sState[k] = "naming" OR sState[k] = "in" THEN
        sState[k] = "closing"
        sSince[k] = SYS.Ticks
        Queue(sTag[k], Chr(1) + "CLOSE")
    END IF
END SUB

SUB DropStandIn (k AS Integer)
    sTag.RemoveAt(k)
    sRoom.RemoveAt(k)
    sOwner.RemoveAt(k)
    sOwnerNick.RemoveAt(k)
    sNick.RemoveAt(k)
    sState.RemoveAt(k)
    sSince.RemoveAt(k)
END SUB

' What a stand-in's connection hears: only its own name matters.
SUB StandInHeard (k AS Integer, tag AS String, msg AS String)
    VAR key AS String
    VAR i AS Integer
    IF msg = Chr(1) + "CONNECTED" THEN
        IF sState[k] = "cancel" THEN
            Forget(tag)
            DropStandIn(k)
        ELSE
            sState[k] = "naming"
            sSince[k] = SYS.Ticks
            SendNow(tag, "NICK " + sNick[k])
        END IF
    ELSEIF msg = Chr(1) + "FAILED" OR msg = Chr(1) + "CLOSED" THEN
        Forget(tag)
        DropStandIn(k)
    ELSEIF msg.StartsWith("OK You are now ") THEN
        IF sState[k] = "naming" THEN
            sState[k] = "in"
            sSince[k] = SYS.Ticks
            Queue(tag, Chr(1) + "JOIN " + channel)
        END IF
    ELSEIF msg.StartsWith("ERR Nick in use") OR msg.StartsWith("ERR Bad nick") THEN
        IF sState[k] <> "naming" AND sState[k] <> "in" THEN RETURN
        ' the name is somebody else's there: tell its owner, once, at home
        key = sOwner[k] + "|" + sOwnerNick[k].Lower() + "|" + sRoom[k]
        clashKey.Add(key)
        clashAt.Add(SYS.Ticks)
        IF NOT told.Contains(key) THEN
            told.Add(key)
            i = mName.IndexOf(sOwner[k])
            IF i >= 0 THEN Say(i, "Somebody on " + Called(sRoom[k]) + " is already called " + sOwnerNick[k] + ", so you can't be heard there. /nick gives you another name.")
            Note(sOwnerNick[k] + "'s name is taken on " + sRoom[k])
        END IF
        EndStandIn(k)
    END IF
END SUB

' Somebody in room i said text: their stand-ins say it in the other rooms.
SUB Relay (i AS Integer, nick AS String, text AS String)
    VAR k AS Integer
    FOR k = 0 TO sTag.Count - 1
        IF sOwner[k] = mName[i] AND sOwnerNick[k].Lower() = nick.Lower() AND sState[k] = "in" THEN Queue(sTag[k], text)
    NEXT
END SUB

' ================================================================ what it says

SUB Say (i AS Integer, text AS String)
    IF i < 0 THEN RETURN
    IF mState[i] <> "in" THEN RETURN
    Queue(mTag[i], text)
END SUB

' Hello, once for each person on each machine.
SUB Greet (i AS Integer, nick AS String)
    VAR key AS String
    VAR names AS Array OF String
    VAR site AS String
    VAR n AS Integer
    IF i < 0 THEN RETURN
    key = mName[i].Split(".")[0] + "|" + nick.Lower()
    IF seen.Contains(key) THEN RETURN
    seen.Add(key)
    FS.Append(HOME + "\SEEN.TXT", key + EOL)
    greeted = greeted + 1
    FOR EACH site IN Sites()
        names.Add(site.Split("|")[0])
    NEXT
    Say(i, "Hi " + nick + ", welcome to SIM95! I'm the greeter bot from " + here.Upper() + ".")
    IF names.Count = 0 THEN
        Say(i, "Open Voyager and go to http://" + here + "/ to see what's on.")
    ELSE
        Say(i, "Open Voyager and go to http://" + here + "/ for " + Listed(names) + ".")
    END IF
    n = Elsewhere(mName[i])
    IF mLinked[i] THEN
        mTold[i] = TRUE
        IF n > 0 THEN
            Say(i, "This room is linked to " + channel + " on every machine: " + Str(n) + " " + People(n) + " elsewhere on the network can talk with you here, and see what you say.")
        ELSE
            Say(i, "This room is linked to " + channel + " on every machine: whoever comes in anywhere on the network will be here too, and see what you say.")
        END IF
    ELSE
        Say(i, "Say link to talk with everybody in " + channel + " across the network (" + Str(n) + " " + People(n) + " now).")
    END IF
    IF IsHub(i) THEN
        Say(i, "Say sites for the list, or who for who's here.")
    ELSEIF mLinked[i] THEN
        Say(i, "Say sites for the list, who for who's here, unlink to keep this room to this machine, or bye and I'll leave it alone.")
    ELSE
        Say(i, "Say sites for the list, or bye and I'll leave this machine alone.")
    END IF
    Note("Greeted " + nick + " on " + mName[i])
END SUB

' Somebody said something in room i: sites, who, link, unlink or bye.
SUB Obey (i AS Integer, nick AS String, text AS String)
    VAR t AS String
    VAR site AS String
    VAR all AS Array OF String
    VAR p AS Array OF String
    VAR k AS Integer
    t = text.Trim().Lower()
    ' "StartHereBot: sites" too
    IF t.StartsWith(mNick[i].Lower()) THEN t = t.Substring(mNick[i].Length, t.Length - mNick[i].Length)
    t = Bare(t)
    IF t = "sites" OR t = "!sites" OR t = "help" THEN
        IF mListed[i] <> 0 AND SYS.Ticks - mListed[i] < QUIET THEN RETURN
        mListed[i] = MATH.Max(1, SYS.Ticks)
        all = Sites()
        IF all.Count = 0 THEN Say(i, "Everything is at http://" + here + "/")
        FOR EACH site IN all
            p = site.Split("|")
            Say(i, p[0] + " - " + p[1] + " - " + p[2])
        NEXT
        Note("Listed the sites for " + nick + " on " + mName[i])
    ELSEIF t = "who" OR t = "!who" THEN
        IF mListed[i] <> 0 AND SYS.Ticks - mListed[i] < QUIET THEN RETURN
        mListed[i] = MATH.Max(1, SYS.Ticks)
        Say(i, WhoLine(i))
    ELSEIF t = "unlink" AND IsHub(i) THEN
        Say(i, "This is where everybody meets: it stays linked.")
    ELSEIF t = "unlink" AND mLinked[i] THEN
        mLinked[i] = FALSE
        FS.Append(HOME + "\UNLINK.TXT", Called(mName[i]) + EOL)
        Say(i, "Unlinked: only people on this machine see this room now. Say link to talk with everybody again.")
        Note(nick + " unlinked " + mName[i])
    ELSEIF t = "link" AND NOT mLinked[i] THEN
        mLinked[i] = TRUE
        FS.Write(HOME + "\UNLINK.TXT", Without(ReadOr(HOME + "\UNLINK.TXT", ""), Called(mName[i])))
        mTold[i] = TRUE
        k = Elsewhere(mName[i])
        Say(i, "Linked: you're in " + channel + " with everybody on the network (" + Str(k) + " " + People(k) + " elsewhere now). Say unlink to undo it.")
        Note(nick + " linked " + mName[i])
    ELSEIF (t = "bye" OR t = "go away" OR t = "leave") AND NOT IsHub(i) THEN
        Say(i, "OK, I'll leave this machine alone. Find us any time at http://" + here + "/ - bye!")
        Queue(mTag[i], Chr(1) + "CLOSE")
        FS.Append(HOME + "\OPTOUT.TXT", Called(mName[i]) + EOL)
        Note(nick + " said bye: leaving " + mName[i] + " alone")
        ' (its connection closes after the goodbye; the rest at once)
        mTag[i] = ""
        RoomDown(i, "left")
    END IF
END SUB

' "Here now: newbie (newbie), regular (starthere)" - everybody in the
' conversation, as this room sees it.
FUNCTION WhoLine (i AS Integer) AS String
    VAR out AS String
    VAR k AS Integer
    VAR n AS Integer
    VAR more AS Integer
    FOR k = 0 TO pRoom.Count - 1
        IF NOT pDone[k] THEN CONTINUE
        IF pRoom[k] <> mName[i] AND NOT (Linked(i) AND Linked(mName.IndexOf(pRoom[k]))) THEN CONTINUE
        IF out.Length > 300 THEN
            more = more + 1
        ELSE
            IF n > 0 THEN out = out + ", "
            out = out + pNick[k] + " (" + Called(pRoom[k]) + ")"
            n = n + 1
        END IF
    NEXT
    IF n = 0 THEN RETURN "Nobody else is here right now."
    IF more > 0 THEN out = out + " and " + Str(more) + " more"
    RETURN "Here now: " + out
END FUNCTION

' Without the bits around a word: ": sites!" -> "sites"
FUNCTION Bare (t AS String) AS String
    WHILE t.Length > 0 AND ":,; ".Contains(t.Substring(0, 1))
        t = t.Substring(1, t.Length - 1)
    END WHILE
    WHILE t.Length > 0 AND "!.? ".Contains(t.Substring(t.Length - 1, 1))
        t = t.Substring(0, t.Length - 1)
    END WHILE
    RETURN t
END FUNCTION

' "SimBook, ColdMail and AskSim"; after six, "and more".
FUNCTION Listed (names AS Array OF String) AS String
    VAR out AS String
    VAR k AS Integer
    IF names.Count = 1 THEN RETURN names[0]
    FOR k = 0 TO MATH.Min(names.Count, 6) - 1
        IF k > 0 THEN
            IF k = names.Count - 1 THEN
                out = out + " and "
            ELSE
                out = out + ", "
            END IF
        END IF
        out = out + names[k]
    NEXT
    IF names.Count > 6 THEN out = out + " and more"
    RETURN out
END FUNCTION

' The sites here, as SimHost's front page lists them: name|address|blurb.
' A folder of C:\WEB with an APP.INF (name|blurb|colour) says how it shows;
' the list below covers apps installed before they wrote one.
FUNCTION Sites () AS Array OF String
    VAR out AS Array OF String
    VAR known AS Array OF String
    VAR f AS String
    VAR k AS String
    VAR p AS Array OF String
    known = ["BOOK|BOOK.SPK|SimBook|The social network: profiles, friends, a news feed, walls, photos and pokes.", "MAIL|MAIL.SPK|ColdMail|Free webmail, with a real mail server behind it.", "ASK|ASK.SPK|AskSim|A search engine with a real crawler that goes round every machine on the network.", "GEO|GEO.SPK|GeoSimies|Free homepages for everybody: neighborhoods, hit counters, guestbooks and webrings.", "WIKI|WIKI.SPK|WikiSim|The encyclopedia: hundreds of articles from Wikipedia, as of 1996.", "ELIZA|BOT.SPK|ELIZA-95|A chatbot with Language-Model-of-Certain-Size manners.", "PAL|PAL.SPK|SimPal|Send and request money in SimBucks.", "TUBE|TUBE.SPK|SimTube|Movies: watch them, put yours up, give them stars.", "STATS|STATS.SPK|SimStats|Web statistics for any site.", "VAPOR|CATALOG.TXT|Vapor|The store: games and every SIM95 program, for your own machine."]
    IF NOT FS.Exists("C:\WEB") THEN RETURN out
    FOR EACH f IN FS.List("C:\WEB")
        IF NOT f.EndsWith("\") THEN CONTINUE
        f = f.Substring(0, f.Length - 1).Upper()
        IF FS.Exists("C:\WEB\" + f + "\APP.INF") THEN
            p = FS.Read("C:\WEB\" + f + "\APP.INF").Trim().Split("|")
            IF p.Count >= 2 THEN
                out.Add(p[0] + "|http://" + here + "/" + f.Lower() + "/|" + p[1])
                CONTINUE
            END IF
        END IF
        FOR EACH k IN known
            p = k.Split("|")
            IF p[0] = f AND FS.Exists("C:\WEB\" + f + "\" + p[1]) THEN out.Add(p[2] + "|http://" + here + "/" + f.Lower() + "/|" + p[3])
        NEXT
    NEXT
    RETURN out
END FUNCTION
